{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant","id":1338018,"title":"Does anyone else feel Changelings make most of Beast: the Primordial seem redundant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-26T12:17:38-07:00","id":1338018,"title":"Does anyone else feel Changelings make most of Beast: the Primordial seem redundant?","content":"It seems to me the whole theme of '<i>fear-eating things that go bump in the night' </i>is covered rather adequately by Darklings and, to a lesser extent, Beasts and Ogres. The only fresh thing BtP brings is the concept of people having their souls replaced by mythical beings, which is quite similar to the old CtL (Beasts remind me a lot of the Thallain), but that's not enough to make it really stand out, imo. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T12:33:24-07:00","id":1338021,"title":"","content":"Ive almost cannibalized everything that i found interesting in Beast for Changeling.<br /> <br /> The two big things i use are Lair rules for Clearings in the Hedge. (Parts of the hedge that intrudes on ironside)<br /> And ive redesigned the horros part of Beast as nightmare gaining sentience and taking over their sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T13:43:49-07:00","id":1338032,"title":"","content":"You might want to... I don't know... put this in the Beast forum if you want Beast fans to add more?<br /> <br /> But no, as someone involved in a mixed game with a Beast, and a Lost game right now, they're more than different enough.<br /> <br /> If there's one simple summation of this? Satiety vs. Clarity. Changeling, without massive house rules, isn't going to get the thematic importance of feeding that Beast has. Yes, the Lost can eat emotions and such, but it's an option they can avoid. Beast isn't going to capture the struggle to maintain a grasp of reality in the face of the way Arcadia was permanently warped the sense of self of Lost.<br /> <br /> There's other things, like Changelings starting as victims and the antagonists being their abusers and those that enable them, vs. Beasts having an enemy that's usually created by Beasts or their allies not actually helping make the world a better place with their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T14:17:53-07:00","id":1338035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant#post1338018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me the whole theme of '<i>fear-eating things that go bump in the night' </i>is covered rather adequately by Darklings and, to a lesser extent, Beasts and Ogres. The only fresh thing BtP brings is the concept of people having their souls replaced by mythical beings, which is quite similar to the old CtL (Beasts remind me a lot of the Thallain), but that's not enough to make it really stand out, imo. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Causing and creating fear I do feel is a specific-enough niche for CtL that you have to go out of your way to stretch and make sense, and enough that it gets away from the core themes of CtL...to the point that I have to ask if you're trying to substitute the themes of CtL with something else, why are you even playing CtL?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T16:56:39-07:00","id":1338069,"title":"","content":"People say Beasts are like Changelings, but they are more like Goetic Sin Eaters, a goetia replaces the space where your soul used to be instead of a Giest. Both have a creepy little buddy and deep inside of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T17:37:17-07:00","id":1338080,"title":"","content":"Changeling does not, as a rule, concern itself too much with controlling the local narrative-space as it relates to its characters' personal occult reputations, nor does the violence of literalized ideological warfare have much in the way of special impact on their place in the world beyond the particulars of personal experience.<br /> <br /> Beast similarly doesn't dedicate too much attention to the process of finding supernatural backing outside the bounds of personal relationships and self-discovery, nor is it especially invested in explicating the details of the metaphysical exchange they make with the subjects of their feeding.<br /> <br /> We had mummies who were vampires years before Mummy: the Curse was announced, but that doesn't make Mummy redundant either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T17:40:10-07:00","id":1338081,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I don't think it's all that redundant - its similar, perhaps, but that's intended. One is a monster who embraces itself - the other is... or perhaps better stated, -was- a human who was made into something they never wanted to be, who now has to come to terms with themselves. Beast is a game that is designed to be played in any system in a crossover setting. If it's themes overlap with other games, that's just means it's serving it's purpose well (it fails most when a beast CAN'T find similarities to a venue, in fact).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I could make a thousand different concepts that could be played in both venues easily, but the themes of each venue would make the end result grossly different, and the story that was told in one would likely look nothing like the story told in another. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As far as changeling already covering the theme of fear-eating things that go bump in the night, I think that really only applies to the autumn court and even then... I feel like it's more like people at Samhain. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Samhain as many probably know was once a festival, where people would light bonfires and wear masks after dark so that the ghosts would think they were fellow spirits. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The changelings in this scenario are the ones who wear masks. The Beasts are the spirits. Sure you can confuse the two, and both are supposed to be frightening - but at the end of the day, one is hiding, and can choose to take that mask off - the other is always a monster.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(Yes, a changeling can't choose not to be a changeling, but they -can- choose not to feed on fear.).</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T21:38:10-07:00","id":1338104,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I've always felt Beast just didn't belong in the CoD. It feels more like a fan-written book to me. Like it's not really its own idea. I don't feel like it's built out of mythology, literature and cinema the same way that the other games are, or at least not like it's built out of one common vein. Character concepts for Beast that I have seen always seem like ones I feel disappointed were used for Beast and not another character type. Plus the way that it connects to all the other lines feels like a fan-written move, something done to kind of ingratiate the newcomer in a way that never really seemed appropriate to me.<br /> <br /> I feel like Deviant suffers from similar issues, but I don't mind it as much in that case. I think that bothers me less because I can see more cinematic and literary connection to Deviant that feels like it would exist in the CoD. I probably wouldn't have made it a major splat, but that's a smaller issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1547,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","user":"BunniRabbi","date":". 09-27-2019, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T22:23:36-07:00","id":1338108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BunniRabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant?p=1338104#post1338104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I've always felt Beast just didn't belong in the CoD. It feels more like a fan-written book to me. Like it's not really its own idea. I don't feel like it's built out of mythology, literature and cinema the same way that the other games are, or at least not like it's built out of one common vein.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corebook was poorly developed. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299553#post1299553\">This has been discussed in the appropriate forum</a>, which this thread is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T22:48:20-07:00","id":1338109,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who was The Changeling Guy and is now one of the Beast Guys* (in the sense of being a local expert on the subject and all of their nuances), Yeah, no. There was a brief period of time where the overlap was more of a thing, but Changeling Second definitively stepped back onto building firmly on First Edition's foundation, and as such Beast has more room to go in it's own direction-which is great, because where that overlap existed for a while <i>honestly</i> serves Beast better than it did Changeling.<br /> <br /> Satchel already did a decent break down of the big differences, so I'll just reiterate it by saying Finding Your Home and Building Your Legend are significantly different angles to approach for stories that are even otherwise identical, and likewise abuse recovery is a different base metaphor from self-transcendence. There's a lot of other nuances that are different as well, but we could be here all day going into it and I have things to do. Maybe once those are done, I'll apply the essayist to the subject.<br /> <br /> THere is still some overlap, of course, since Beast should be raw enough to work well in a crossover capacity, but that sort of overlap is the same across the board-Beast has just as much in common with Vampire as it does Changeling**.<br /> <br /> *Cinder being THE Beast Guy.<br /> **If you really wanted me to composite the two games I'd smush together to get the next-best facsimile of Beast, I'd more put money on Werewolf and Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-27-2019, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T16:23:16-07:00","id":1338205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant#post1338018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me the whole theme of '<i>fear-eating things that go bump in the night' </i>is covered rather adequately by Darklings and, to a lesser extent, Beasts and Ogres. The only fresh thing BtP brings is the concept of people having their souls replaced by mythical beings, which is quite similar to the old CtL (Beasts remind me a lot of the Thallain), but that's not enough to make it really stand out, imo. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. My best media example for a beast is Showtimes' Dexter. In particular Dexter and the Dark Passenger, how it seems like a living thing that is coiled around him, is him, consumes him it has needs of it's own and it sustains and supports dexter to ensure he can continue to feed it. He tempers the darkness but it is in control. This is the perfect analogy for a beast.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a changeling doesn't have the drive, the need, it wants to do these things. I can stop when ever it wants, it can become human again. It doesn't have a voice in its ear howling about how hungry it is, how they need to kill.<br /> Both can deal with themes of fear but they do it much differently and with very different attitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T16:36:00-07:00","id":1338207,"title":"","content":"I don't think it makes the game redundant but I appreciate where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> One of the things that drew me to Changeling (first edition) was the idea of being able to make any kind of monster, effectively being able to emulate a vampire, werewolf, wizard (at least theoretically), golem, whatever. And Beast seems to have taken that mantle on its own (though as we see in Deviant and hinted in other things it may be part of a larger shift in concepts), while also grabbing a narrower part of Changeling (Changelings, even in the Autumn court, don't have to harvest fear, they just get a bonus for it) and making it more central.<br /> <br /> The idea of later games adapting aspects of earlier games is just a part of growth, however, and is inevitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-27-2019, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T18:13:15-07:00","id":1338215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant?p=1338205#post1338205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. My best media example for a beast is Showtimes' Dexter. In particular Dexter and the Dark Passenger, how it seems like a living thing that is coiled around him, is him, consumes him it has needs of it's own and it sustains and supports dexter to ensure he can continue to feed it. He tempers the darkness but it is in control. This is the perfect analogy for a beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off topic: I read your above post too quickly and assumed that it was about Dexter's Lab, the cartoon. This provided a very interesting take on his lab as a Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T18:26:48-07:00","id":1338362,"title":"","content":"I think the main parallels that made me less interested in Beast was less the fear aspect and more the playing with dreams and especially the idea of drawing power from and being trapped with a story. I loved that aspect of changeling and seeing elements of it crop up in Beast did steer me away from that game. <br /> <br /> Also I was a little weirded out by the parallels with Beast and Changeling. No not that Changeling the other Changeling! Old school Changeling the Dreaming. Both those games featured dream entities living within human hosts who believed they had a kinship with all the other things that go bump in the darkness. I\u2019m not saying it was a huge deal but it definitely contributed to my overall lack of interest. The setting didn\u2019t feel as fresh as it might have. <br /> <br /> Also, really getting into nitpick territory but I wish they found a name that wasn\u2019t already a splat in changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T19:34:00-07:00","id":1338370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant?p=1338362#post1338362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main parallels that made me less interested in Beast was less the fear aspect and more the playing with dreams and especially the idea of drawing power from and being trapped with a story. I loved that aspect of changeling and seeing elements of it crop up in Beast did steer me away from that game.<br /> <br /> Also I was a little weirded out by the parallels with Beast and Changeling. No not that Changeling the other Changeling! Old school Changeling the Dreaming. Both those games featured dream entities living within human hosts who believed they had a kinship with all the other things that go bump in the darkness. I\u2019m not saying it was a huge deal but it definitely contributed to my overall lack of interest. The setting didn\u2019t feel as fresh as it might have.<br /> <br /> Also, really getting into nitpick territory but I wish they found a name that wasn\u2019t already a splat in changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a fair amount of overlap one way or another. A properly executed Beast is, in a stupidly simplistic sense, Scion-but-Chronicles-of-Darkness.<br /> <br /> Albeit, it has a lot of room to be weirder than that, but the general gist is there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T00:47:57-07:00","id":1338411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant?p=1338362#post1338362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I was a little weirded out by the parallels with Beast and Changeling. No not that Changeling the other Changeling! Old school Changeling the Dreaming. Both those games featured dream entities living within human hosts who believed they had a kinship with all the other things that go bump in the darkness. I\u2019m not saying it was a huge deal but it definitely contributed to my overall lack of interest. The setting didn\u2019t feel as fresh as it might have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that was never too surprising to me.<br /> <br /> The line dev for Beast was also the line dev for the Changeling: the Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition. I honestly wouldn't be surprised if Beast was meant to be a way to bring in elements of Dreaming into CofD that Lost didn't already cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T05:16:16-07:00","id":1338440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant?p=1338370#post1338370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a fair amount of overlap one way or another. A properly executed Beast is, in a stupidly simplistic sense, Scion-but-Chronicles-of-Darkness.<br /> <br /> Albeit, it has a lot of room to be weirder than that, but the general gist is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth. Reduced to core elements (which admittedly ignore lots of differences, themes and plenty of elements esclusive to each other) the skeleton of Beast and Scion are made of similar bones. <br /> <br /> It's how they're arranged and the flesh upon them that changes. But that's a whole different big discussion.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd say Primordial is closer to Scion and Dreaming than it is to 2E Lost (for reasons others already covered). Which is a good thing, mind you: gives more breathing room for both games to exist in a single setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T05:34:51-07:00","id":1338443,"title":"","content":"Now that you say that i think i wouldve really loved for Beast to focus more on this aspect.<br /> The idea that the horror wants its legend to spread, gets stronger and more defined the more people talk about it. This interest me much more than the hunger aspect currently.<br /> This would also make for a nice contrast and interesting interactions with the rest of CofD cast who all prefer to stay hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T05:54:42-07:00","id":1338447,"title":"","content":"There's more about building your legend in the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> I think that touches on a problem that Beast and other lines have, or had in their first edition, which is that the core book spends a lot of time on the basic existential threats a splat faces. These are all the reasons that being X is difficult and scary and likely to end badly. They're geared for starting characters, and there's only so much in the way of word count to spend detailing advanced options. Then the supplements are free to dig into the question of 'ok, you survived your first few threats and have something approaching a sustainable routine, where do you go now that you have room to look beyond the next meal?'<br /> <br /> It makes sense to build the foundation that way, but it also sometimes leaves prospective players with a first impression that the stories are more limited than is actually the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T01:19:31-07:00","id":1338588,"title":"","content":"The Beats Actually remind Changelings of the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T04:06:40-07:00","id":1338599,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that that's only in part, and more superficial than not. Beasts in other Realms (including the Hedge) have a stronger impact due to their Horror's influence than is normal outside of high Wyrd Lost and Gentry, like the Gentry they have an aptitude to poke around in dreams, and plenty of Beasts are as abusive as Keepers are.<br /> <br /> If a Beast and a changeling sit down and chat about it, it would be pretty clear that the Begotten are distinct from the Gentry in a bunch of major ways; not that the Lost will necessarily care about this when considering the Beast a threat or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}